※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4526

※ Arguments written without a name fill the parameters from the left, so a
※ parameter with a default before one without means a call one argument short
※ cannot say which one it left out.  Every parameter after one with a default
※ has one too -- the rule C++, Python, D and Swift all state.  Naming the
※ arguments is what gets round it at the call, but the rule is about what a
※ call written without names can mean.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = plus(1u8, 2u8)
    0u6

fn plus(n: u8 ← 1u8, by: u8) → u8:
    n + by
